WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.970
[MUSIC]

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:11.563
Exceptional leaders,
the ones who come to mind when you think

00:00:11.563 --> 00:00:15.184
about people you admire is
that they are known for

00:00:15.184 --> 00:00:19.443
continuing their development
throughout their lives.

00:00:19.443 --> 00:00:24.838
Folks who take a growth mindset,
see the challenges they're

00:00:24.838 --> 00:00:30.442
facing as something that they
could develop enough to achieve or

00:00:30.442 --> 00:00:33.464
overcome or master or learn from.

00:00:33.464 --> 00:00:39.265
So that a failure from a growth mindset
perspective is an opportunity to learn.

00:00:39.265 --> 00:00:41.952
The typical approach is to be judgmental,

00:00:41.952 --> 00:00:45.610
to think of what's happening
as somehow inevitable, and

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:50.550
then to worry about assigning blame for
all those things that are going wrong.

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:57.054
If we can develop more of a growth
mindset, we can do a much better job

00:00:57.054 --> 00:01:02.130
of creating in ourselves a set
of capabilities that can make

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:07.530
us more successful precisely because
we've run into difficulties in the past.

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:10.720
So at all levels,
exceptional leadership for

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:15.170
you as an individual, for the organization
of the people you touch there and for

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:19.010
the world all have to do with whether or

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:23.630
not you take a developmental approach or
a judgemental approach.

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:29.420
How do your actions as a leader
affect the growth mindset of others?

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:31.480
What can you do to make it so

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:36.480
that your workplace is more
developmental and less judgemental?

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:43.200
&gt;&gt; Question your assumptions and
explore new approaches to leadership.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.263
Explore Stanford's upcoming programs.

00:01:46.263 --> 00:01:50.085
[MUSIC]

